# Public UI

Routes: `/`, `/calendar`, `/form`, `/success`, `/sd-form`, `/bookings/:id/parking` (pay parking).

No admin auth required. Branding via property scope (`?property=<slug>`).

## Layout

`MainLayout` — guest nav; `KameFormBrandHeader` on form flows.

## Calendar → form

`CalendarPage` preserves query params (`?source=airbnb`, `?property=`) when navigating to `/form`.

## Guest form

| Concern      | Location                                              |
| ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| Main UI      | `ui/src/features/guest/form/components/GuestForm.tsx` |
| Schema       | `guestFormSchema.ts`                                  |
| Submit       | `submit-form` edge function (FormData)                |
| Booked dates | `get-booked-dates`                                    |

Production: full save path. Non-prod / `?dev=true`: dev checkbox panel (save DB, storage, calendar, sheet, email).

## SD refund

`/sd-form?bookingId=` — `get-sd-form` read-only; `submit-sd-form` + `claim-sd-voucher` at `READY_FOR_CHECKOUT`.

## Pay parking

`/bookings/:bookingId/parking` — owner broadcast flow; separate from main guest form.

## API calls

Use `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` + anon key. Pass `?property=` or `?property_id=` when scoped.

## UX

- Mobile-first (375px)
- Minimal copy (`ui-minimal-copy.mdc`)
- Guide: `docs/guides/routes/form.md`, `calendar.md`, `sd-form.md`

## Don'ts

- Require Google sign-in on public routes
- Expose admin URLs or service role in guest bundle
- Block guest submit on optional dev-only code paths in production builds
